Negative control for the ONE-ACTIONS-LIST law (`R6-33`).

Draws the whole declared list on every record, so the collection's own control —
the one fired with NO row, which is why it sits in the page header (G4) — is
offered per row as well. The single channel is kept; what is withdrawn is the
placement that tells the two apart, which is the only thing that ever
distinguished them once `rowActions`/`collectionActions` collapsed.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the list-surface action specs — a header-placed action is drawn once, in
the page header, and never among a row's own controls.

